  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A balanced parenthesis string is defined as follows:\n\n\nThe empty string is balanced.\nIf PPP is balanced, (P)(P)(P) is also balanced.\nIf PPP and QQQ are balanced, PQPQPQ is also balanced.\nYou are given two even integers nnn and kkk. Find any balanced parenthesis string of length nnn that doesn't contain a balanced substring of length kkk, or claim that no such string exists.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nEach test case consists of a single line containing nnn and kkk.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor every test case, print on a new line, any balanced parenthesis string of length nnn that doesn't contain a balanced substring of length kkk. If there doesn't exist any such string, print −1-1−1 instead.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤500001 \\leq T \\leq 500001≤T≤50000",
      "2≤k≤n≤1052 \\leq k \\leq n \\leq 10^52≤k≤n≤105",
      "Sum of nnn over all test cases doesn't exceed 10510^5105.",
      "nnn and kkk are both even integers."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n4 2\n8 6",
        "output": "-1\n(())(())",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nIn the first test case, the only balanced strings of length 444 are (()) and ()(), both of which contain () as a substring.\nIn the second test case, (())(()) is a balanced string that doesn't contain any balanced substring of length 666."
      }
    ]
  },
